Rem ==================================================================
Rem sparky-core.shoddy — the dictionary an MCP client is handed, with
Rem nothing that touches the world.
Rem
Rem Pure. Nothing here reads a file, writes one or prints. What this file
Rem owns is a fold — which seeds a Sparky session starts from — and the
Rem handful of words a host has to answer for itself. Everything else is
Rem reckoner's and the seed files'.
Rem
Rem WHY THIS IS A MILL AND NOT A NARROWER GRANT OVER HALIFAX. A
Rem capability grant does not gate a dictionary: withholding `scribbler`
Rem from halifax would leave SCRIBOPEN registered, listed by WORDS,
Rem answered by HELP, and returning null-seam nonsense to whoever called
Rem it. The seed fold is the ONLY mechanism that decides which words
Rem exist, and a fold is a mill's own code. So the honest way to hand a
Rem model a smaller dictionary is a smaller fold, which is this file.
Rem
Rem THE FOLD IS HALIFAX'S, LESS THREE. SpkFresh below is HxFresh with
Rem three lines deleted and nothing reordered, so WORDS groups the words
Rem in the order a reader of halifax's listing already knows. The three:
Rem
Rem   seedbuzzer — sound. The server does not control the host's audio
Rem                lifetime, cannot know whether anything is listening,
Rem                and has no use for it.
Rem   seedkeys   — pure, and pointless. It classifies keystrokes and
Rem                there is no keystroke source anywhere in this mill.
Rem   seedvt100  — pure, and pointless. It builds escape sequences for a
Rem                screen that does not exist; a client receiving them
Rem                in JSON is worse off than one told the word is
Rem                absent.
Rem
Rem A seed is never folded in part. Each of the three is excluded whole
Rem or not at all, and mills/sparky/test.shoddy asserts both directions —
Rem that every seed halifax folds is here bar those three, and that none
Rem of those three's words can be reached.
Rem
Rem THERE IS NO INPUT WORD TO EXCLUDE. seedbuiltin bridges no reading
Rem builtin and seedterminal registers PRINT and only PRINT, so INPUT,
Rem INPUTLINE and INKEY are already absent from every reckoner
Rem dictionary. This paragraph exists so a later reader does not go
Rem looking for a suppression that was never needed.
Rem
Rem ---- THIS FILE DOES NOT INCLUDE halifax-core.shoddy ----------------
Rem
Rem Deliberately, and it is the decision most likely to be undone by
Rem someone tidying. Halifax's Hx layer is a terminal REPL: a prompt, a
Rem banner, QUIT, a continuation buffer, and the interception that lets
Rem SAVE mean something when typed as a whole line. Sparky's caller is a
Rem model calling tools, and its door is the engine's own — RckEval,
Rem which reckoner.shoddy calls "the only door a shell needs". Borrowing
Rem the REPL would import a prompt model there is no prompt for.
Rem
Rem ---- THE WORDS THE HOST OWNS ---------------------------------------
Rem
Rem SAVE, LOAD, TAPESAVE and RESET are registered here for their
Rem metadata alone, exactly as halifax registers its own: what
Rem registration buys is that WORDS lists them and HELP SAVE answers.
Rem A dictionary whose persistence is invisible to the two words someone
Rem explores with has hidden part of itself.
Rem
Rem THEIR BODIES REFUSE, and here the refusal is the ordinary outcome
Rem rather than a should-never-happen. Halifax intercepts the typed line
Rem before it reaches RckEval, so its stub only runs when the
Rem interception failed. Sparky has no line to intercept: a client asks
Rem for a save by CALLING THE SAVE TOOL, and a line arriving at RckEval
Rem with SAVE in it is someone reaching for the wrong door. So the
Rem message names the door that does work rather than telling them to
Rem retype the line.
Rem
Rem QUIT AND EXIT ARE NOT REGISTERED AT ALL. A server has no session to
Rem leave, and a word whose help described leaving would describe
Rem something that cannot happen. Their absence is a fact about this
Rem dictionary and test.shoddy asserts it.
Rem ==================================================================

Include "../../machines/seq.shoddy"
Include "../../machines/reckoner.shoddy"
Include "../../machines/seeds/seedbuiltin.shoddy"
Include "../../machines/seeds/seedmath.shoddy"
Include "../../machines/seeds/seedstats.shoddy"
Include "../../machines/seeds/seedseq.shoddy"
Include "../../machines/seeds/seedstr.shoddy"
Include "../../machines/seeds/seedmoney.shoddy"
Include "../../machines/seeds/seedmatrix.shoddy"
Include "../../machines/seeds/seeddict.shoddy"
Include "../../machines/seeds/seedfile.shoddy"
Include "../../machines/seeds/seedclock.shoddy"
Include "../../machines/seeds/seedrandom.shoddy"
Include "../../machines/seeds/seedcsv.shoddy"
Include "../../machines/seeds/seedbool.shoddy"
Include "../../machines/seeds/seedshaker.shoddy"
Include "../../machines/seeds/seedjson.shoddy"
Include "../../machines/seeds/seedxml.shoddy"
Include "../../machines/seeds/seedhtml.shoddy"
Include "../../machines/seeds/seedsimplex.shoddy"
Include "../../machines/seeds/seedlin.shoddy"
Include "../../machines/seeds/seedeng.shoddy"
Include "../../machines/seeds/seedfin.shoddy"
Include "../../machines/seeds/seedalg.shoddy"
Include "../../machines/seeds/seedneural.shoddy"
Include "../../machines/seeds/seedrecio.shoddy"
Include "../../machines/seeds/seedisam.shoddy"
Include "../../machines/seeds/seedscribbler.shoddy"
Include "../../machines/seeds/seednet.shoddy"
Include "../../machines/seeds/seedturtle.shoddy"
Include "../../machines/seeds/seedplotter.shoddy"
Include "../../machines/seeds/seedhttps.shoddy"
Include "../../machines/seeds/seedregex.shoddy"
